llama.cpp (as fetched by Ollama v0.35.1, llama.cpp b11232): faster single-token
matmuls for K-quant and low-bit IQ models on gfx803.

WHY
---
Token generation reads every weight once per token, so it should run at the
card's memory bandwidth. On an RX 590 it does for q8_0 and f16 weights
(test-backend-ops perf, MUL_MAT n=1, 4096x14336: q8_0 222 GB/s, f16 229 GB/s,
about the practical limit), but not for the K-quants that make up a Q4_K_M
model: q4_K reaches 127-160 GB/s depending on shape, q6_K 165 GB/s. gfx803 has
no integer dot product instructions, so their dot products are long ALU
sequences and the kernel is instruction-bound, not memory-bound. Registers are
not the limit (34 VGPRs, no spills).

The GCN parameter table launches two warps per output row for one column. On
gfx803, one warp over two rows is faster for these types: each row's partial
sums need half the cross-warp reduction, launches halve, and each wave keeps
two rows' loads in flight. Per matmul (4096x14336 unless noted): q3_K +31%,
q4_K +11% (+19-27% for the 4096-14336 row shapes), q2_K +11%, q6_K +9%, iq1_m
+24%, iq1_s +16%, iq2_xxs/xs/s +7-11%, mxfp4 +9%, nvfp4 +30%, q2_0 +11%. q5_K
(-7%), q8_0, iq4_xs and q5_1 (-2-3%) are slower that way and keep the GCN
shape; the remaining types are unchanged within noise.

llama-bench token generation, q8_0 KV cache, flash attention, depth 0/4k/8k:
Qwen3 8B Q4_K_M 27.9/25.7/24.2 -> 31.2/28.6/26.5 tok/s, Qwen2.5-Coder 7B
Q4_K_M 30.3/28.6/27.0 -> 34.2/32.3/30.1. Prompt processing is unaffected (the
change applies only to the one-column decode path).

WHAT
----
A GCN4 entry in mmvq's parameter table, selected for gfx803 only (device code
by the GCN4 define, host code by GGML_CUDA_CC_GCN4). For one column it uses one
warp and two rows per block for the types listed in mmvq_gcn4_two_rows() and
the GCN shape for all others; every other column count is the GCN table's.
Other GCN and CDNA GPUs keep the GCN table.

Checked against the CPU backend with test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT 1301/1301,
MUL_MAT_ID 931/931 (the forced two-row shape for every type passes the same
suites).

